    description: "**Origin.** Filed 2026-05-30 as a sub-META of INV-fabov following the linked-pile L1 investigation. Sub-META C.\n\n**The shape.** Five active items describe \"value must be in a known registry but isn't checked.\" A CLI flag accepts arbitrary strings as the value of a flag whose semantics require a registry lookup (language catalog, framework catalog, section vocabulary, view vocabulary). When the string isn't a registry member, the subcommand proceeds (silently producing empty/wrong output) rather than rejecting with a helpful \"did you mean…\" hint.\n\n**Fix shape.** A shared argparse `choices=` wiring backed by the relevant catalog/registry, plus a small fuzzy-match helper for `--did-you-mean` suggestion text. Each member item is one subcommand × one registry binding.\n\n**Members (5).** INV-gufod (config silently accepts framework/linker names as if they were languages), INV-gapib (all --input consumers silently accept wrong-view JSON), INV-subak (config --format json: function_summaries empty for ALL 281 languages — the \"281\" is the silent-accept artifact; non-language framework IDs return empty JSON), INV-votop (search --kind, --language registry violations — primary face; --limit type-range face is cross-referenced to sub-META B), WI-furop (sketch --require-section silently accepts invalid section names).\n\n**Parent:** INV-fabov-kapit-mupit-tigoz-lurol-mulus-jivik-kajun."  # 86ff
    fields:  # 86ff
      statement: "Every CLI flag whose semantics require a registry lookup (language catalog, framework catalog, section vocabulary, view vocabulary) must reject non-registry values with a helpful did-you-mean hint; no such flag may proceed silently on a non-registry value."  # 86ff
      root_cause: "argparse choices= is not wired through to relevant catalogs at the 5 affected sites. Symptoms: config accepts framework/linker names as if languages (INV-gufod), --input consumers accept wrong-view JSON (INV-gapib), config --format json accepts non-language framework IDs returning empty (INV-subak), search accepts invalid --kind/--language (INV-votop), sketch --require-section accepts invalid section names (WI-furop)."  # 86ff
